Subject: [PATCH 2/7] T22: stage-0 protocol, selected-band predeclaration
 (B=9), amendments A1-A4

Stage-0 protocol (plan/T22_STAGE0_PROTOCOL_2026-09-11.md + its JSON, the single
configuration source the runner reads) resolves audit items (a)-(g) and prompt
items 1-7 before any T22 code was written.

Selected-band freeze: B = 9 by the declared smallest-within-one-bootstrap-sd
rule over four eligible development stretches; b_eval = 32, b_cal = 8;
dependence verdict INCONCLUSIVE, which by amendment A3 withholds all three
benefit verdicts.  Validation 0012/0013/0014, final test 0015-0019 (0016 chirped
in the new time region, excluded from combined estimates, leaving four eligible).
Development spent 176 of the 250 fit cap.

Amendments, all recorded before the affected outcomes:
A1 development set 3 -> 6 stretches (only one of the three original ones is
   eligible-coupled at w=65536); nominal fits 184 -> 240, cap unchanged.
A2 evaluation block grid gains 32 (nine complete blocks at 300 windows).
A3 the dependence withholding rule applies to all three benefit verdicts, and
   the primary combined interval becomes a two-stage bootstrap carrying
   within-file uncertainty.
A4 the second-line admissibility test is restated as a local-maximum test beyond
   a one-bin guard.  The first form compared observed band power against the
   idealised boxcar Dirichlet skirt and rejected every band of width >= 3 on
   three of four development stretches; the measured profiles decay
   monotonically outward on both sides -- leakage, not a second line -- but sit
   ~4x above the idealisation.  Development was re-scored once with identical
   seeds; all contrasts reproduce exactly (0 differences).

