+\section{Instrument evidence}
+\label{sec:mlst-instruments}
+
+\subsection{Three instruments, three questions}
+\label{subsec:mlst-instrument-table}
+
+No public release answers every question the theory raises, and the three used
+here answer different ones.  Table~\ref{tab:mlst-instruments} states, for each
+release, which of three questions it can and cannot decide: whether the
+reconstruction improves \emph{in the assumed geometry}; whether the
+\emph{assumed covariance is calibrated} on that data; and whether the
+reconstruction agrees with \emph{recorded truth in a named metric}.  Detection
+sensitivity is not among them and is not claimed anywhere in this paper.
+
+\begin{table}[!htbp]
+\centering
+\small
+\caption{What each public release can and cannot answer.  ``--'' marks a
+question the release cannot pose, not a test that failed.  Untested quantities
+are named as such; detection sensitivity is not claimed for any release.}
+\label{tab:mlst-instruments}
+\begin{tabular}{@{}p{0.16\linewidth}p{0.25\linewidth}p{0.25\linewidth}p{0.25\linewidth}@{}}
+\toprule
+& \textbf{Q1.} Fixed-rank weighted risk: does covariance weighting lower the held-out weighted residual at matched rank?
+& \textbf{Q2.} Noise calibration: is the assumed covariance calibrated on this data?
+& \textbf{Q3.} Named physical truth metric: does it agree with recorded truth? \\
+\midrule
+\textbf{CRESST-II/III} pulse shapes &
+\emph{Yes, positive.}  EMPCA lower in all 7 channels; equal-channel mean $21.6\%$, hierarchical 95\% CI $[10.3,38.8]\%$ &
+\emph{Not tested.}  A stationary PSD with shrinkage $0.1$ is assumed, not validated &
+\emph{--}\ No recorded truth: residuals only \\
+\addlinespace
+\textbf{GWOSC} O1 H1/L1 &
+\emph{Not the question asked.}  Used as a calibration stress test &
+\emph{Yes, negative.}  Global and local-64\,s PSD models fail the null-spread gate on both detectors (up to $10.5$); implementation checks pass &
+\emph{--}\ No injected reference \\
+\addlinespace
+\textbf{TIDMAD} validation files &
+\emph{Yes, in direction only.}  Band-EMPCA below band-PCA; at the whole window the margin is small beside the gap to a bin read &
+\emph{Yes, positive, second moments only.}  $\chi^{2}$/dof $1.0031$, score dispersion $1.0142$ in $[0.9,1.1]$; no tails, dependence or coverage &
+\emph{Yes.}  Injected reference channel; scored as squared injected-amplitude error in readout units.  \textbf{Whole window: no useful recovery} (Sec.~\ref{subsec:mlst-tidmad}); narrowband: Sec.~\ref{subsec:mlst-t22} \\
+\bottomrule
+\end{tabular}
+\end{table}
+
+\subsection{CRESST: within-channel reconstruction}
+\label{subsec:mlst-cresst}
+
+The public CRESST-II/III pulse-shape release
+\citep{angloher2025cresstpulshape,angloher2023datacleaning} supplies seven
+run/channel pairs, each treated independently and split chronologically
+(70\% calibration, 30\% evaluation), with pulse and noise streams split
+separately; no evaluation pulse entered a fitted object, and within-stream row
+and trace-hash overlap is zero.  The pooled held-out comparison is 19{,}335
+pulses.  The frozen model is rank-6 EMPCA with a stationary PSD covariance and
+shrinkage $0.1$; the learned models are affine ($\mu+P(x-\mu)$) while
+single-template OF is a line through zero.
+
+\emph{The same-rank contrast is the covariance-weighting evidence.}  Holding
+rank at six, EMPCA had the lower channel-mean weighted residual in \emph{all
+seven} channels, with fractional reduction $1-R_{\mathrm{EMPCA}}/R_{\mathrm{PCA}}$
+from $1.6\%$ to $62.0\%$ and an equal-channel mean of $21.6\%$; the
+hierarchical 95\% interval for that estimand is $[10.3,38.8]\%$
+(channel-fixed $[17.4,27.1]\%$, ratio-of-means sensitivity $[12.1,39.8]\%$,
+block lengths 16--256 moving it by under $0.35$ points), from a
+channel-then-event bootstrap with 10{,}000 replicates.  All seven channel
+effects are individually positive with intervals excluding zero, and nearly all
+the uncertainty is channel-level.  This is a \emph{sensitivity analysis of the
+archive, not an independent replication}: seven channels from two runs are
+seven correlated clusters, one operating point, one rank, one shrinkage.
+
+\emph{The signal-model contrast is capacity, not geometry.}  Rank-6 EMPCA also
+beat single-template OF in every channel, by an equal-channel fractional
+reduction of $96.2\%$, and met the multi-template competitiveness gate
+everywhere.  That contrast is an order of magnitude larger than the same-rank
+one and primarily measures replacing a fixed template with a rank-6 model; it
+is not evidence about covariance weighting, and we keep the two apart for that
+reason.  All five negative controls degraded at the pooled level; the weakest,
+wrong-PSD weighting, has two of seven channel intervals including zero.
+
+The tied-AE row deserves its caveat: at the archived commit the CRESST path
+evaluates the tied autoencoder through its closed form, which delegates to the
+same weighted-PCA routine that fits EMPCA.  Its maximum principal angle of
+$1.91\times10^{-6}$ degrees is a \emph{parameterization-consistency check of
+two code paths}, not an independently optimized model.  The independent
+optimizer check is the synthetic gate S3.
+
+\subsection{GWOSC: a calibration boundary}
+\label{subsec:mlst-gwosc}
+
+Public 4-kHz H1/L1 strain around GW150914
+\citep{gwoscgw150914,abbott2021opendata} was used as a stress test, not an
+event search: one 256-second interval, 62 valid off-source windows per
+detector, a Hann-windowed bias-corrected median-Welch PSD from calibration
+windows, and template-score dispersion on held-out windows over five random and
+five chronological splits, with a null spread near one as the target.
+
+The implementation checks passed and the calibration tests did not.  PSD ratios
+against GWpy \citep{macleod2021gwpy} were one at recorded precision and the
+shared-FIR paths agreed to $\sim10^{-13}$, far below tolerance; yet the global
+PSD failed the aggregate random and chronological gates for both detectors,
+with individual null-spread ratios reaching $10.480$ (H1) and $7.619$ (L1), and
+the predeclared 64-second local model passed its stationary synthetic control
+($1.148$) but failed on real H1 and L1 ($9.424$, $8.827$).  Event scores and
+nominal injections remain archived diagnostics; they are not converted to
+significance, false-alarm probability or sensitivity.
+
+This is a boundary result, not a verdict on the geometry, and it motivates the
+next stage: because GWOSC carries no injected reference, a calibration failure
+there cannot be separated from the question the theory asks.  A
+structurally wrong covariance model, moreover, need not have a large
+$\varepsilon$ and its $\varepsilon$ does not shrink with more calibration data
+(Section~\ref{subsec:mlst-local}).
+
+\subsection{TIDMAD: recovery against recorded truth at the whole window}
+\label{subsec:mlst-tidmad}
+
+The TIDMAD release from the ABRACADABRA axion search \citep{fry2024tidmad}
+records an injected reference channel alongside the SQUID readout at 10~MHz, so
+a reconstruction can be scored against a real injected signal in real detector
+noise.  A redesigned protocol, predeclared and executed once, asked the
+recovery question on untouched data.  Its endpoint is the physical injected
+amplitude in readout units, $a=2q/\sqrt{w}$ with $q$ the unitary-DFT
+coefficient at the injection bin, so window lengths are comparable; its truth
+label transfers the reference coefficient to readout units through a complex
+gain fitted on 64 disjoint transfer-calibration windows per stretch; every
+stretch is characterized (line, drift, coupling, multi-tone) on those
+calibration windows \emph{before any method is fitted}; and the usefulness
+criterion is predeclared --- an estimator is useful only if it beats both the
+zero predictor and the calibration-mean predictor with 95\% intervals excluding
+zero.  Three development files selected $w=65536$ at rank~2, three validation
+files confirmed the direction, and the final test ran once on fourteen files,
+of which eight were eligible-coupled.
+
+\emph{There is no useful recovery at this operating point.}  Over the eleven
+eligible stretches rank-2 PCA and EMPCA are indistinguishable from predicting
+zero (mean amplitude RMSE $0.661$ and $0.655$ against $0.654$) and about
+$2.7\times$ worse than reading the injection bin with no denoising ($0.246$).
+The combined paired contrasts of EMPCA against both usefulness references
+include zero ($+1.6\times10^{-5}$ $[-8.9\times10^{-5},+1.2\times10^{-4}]$ and
+$+4.6\times10^{-4}$ $[-3.8\times10^{-5},+9.6\times10^{-4}]$), while the bin
+read beats EMPCA at $-1.19\times10^{-2}$
+$[-1.31\times10^{-2},-1.08\times10^{-2}]$.  No ``useful'' verdict was issued
+anywhere --- both because the criterion fails on its own terms and because the
+frozen block-dependence assessment was inconclusive at nine evaluation blocks,
+which by the declared rule withholds it.
+
+Three further facts are recorded.  EMPCA does beat PCA consistently, in the
+direction the metric predicts, and the diagnostic shows why: it places
+$2.8\times10^{-3}$ of its reconstruction energy at the injection bin against
+PCA's $2.1\times10^{-4}$ --- an order of magnitude more, still not enough to
+compete with the bin itself.  The quadrature-OF and bin-read estimators agree
+to $2.6\times10^{-13}$ on all eligible stretches, confirming the
+diagonal-Fourier-weighting identity on real data.  And the precision-weighted
+combined estimate is \emph{effectively one file}: \texttt{0019}, whose injected
+amplitudes are the smallest and whose bootstrap standard deviation is therefore
+the narrowest, carries $98.65\%$ of the inverse-variance weight, while the
+equal-file mean is $+7.8\times10^{-3}$ (Fig.~\ref{fig:mlst-tidmad-perfile}).
+Two post-hoc sensitivities on the eight eligible files agree about scale and
+differ about sign: an equal-file mean with a file-level $t$-interval,
+$+7.8\times10^{-3}$ $[-4.2\times10^{-3},+2.0\times10^{-2}]$, includes zero; a
+DerSimonian--Laird random-effects combination, $+6.5\times10^{-3}$
+$[+1.9\times10^{-3},+1.1\times10^{-2}]$, excludes it.  With eight files and
+$I^{2}\approx0.98$ neither replaces the predeclared primary, which stands as
+executed.
+
+\emph{The leading hypothesis for the cause is dimensional, and it is stated as
+a hypothesis.}  At $w=65536$ the real-view dimension is $p=65536$ against
+$n=350$ fit windows, $p/n=187$.  In the spiked-covariance model a population
+spike must exceed the noise level by about $\sqrt{p/n}\approx14$ before the
+leading sample eigenvector overlaps it, and the injected tone's bin power is
+about $25$ times the noise floor --- near that threshold rather than clearly
+beyond it, and the measured bin SNR is not a population spike in any case.
+What is measured is the outcome: the injection bin carries $1.65\times10^{-3}$
+of the window energy while PCA's rank-2 reconstruction places
+$2.1\times10^{-4}$ there, an under-representation of about $8\times$.  Whether
+estimation error in the whole-window subspace is the cause is what a narrowband
+representation at the same window length is designed to decide.
+
+\begin{figure}[!htbp]
+    \centering
+    \includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{generated/figures/fig_tidmad_perfile.pdf}
+    \caption{TIDMAD held-out operating-range test, per file ($w=65536$,
+    rank~2).  (a)~The paired contrast $\overline{\Delta}(\text{zero},\text{EMPCA})$
+    on each of the fourteen final-test files, ordered by injection frequency,
+    with its joint calibration/evaluation block-bootstrap 95\% interval; a
+    positive value favours EMPCA over predicting zero.  The dashed line is the
+    unweighted mean of the eight eligible files; the precision-weighted
+    estimate coincides with file \texttt{0019}.  (b)~Inverse-variance weight
+    shares.  (c)~Mean amplitude RMSE by method over the eleven eligible
+    stretches: the learned rank-2 reconstructions sit at the trivial-predictor
+    level (dotted), the frequency-domain estimators at $0.24$--$0.25$.
+    Exported at full precision from the archived stage outputs by
+    \nolinkurl{scripts/export_tidmad_heldout.py}; see
+    \nolinkurl{evidence/data/paper1/mlst_2026-09-11/README.md}.}
+    \label{fig:mlst-tidmad-perfile}
+\end{figure}
+
