+# T22 stage-0 protocol — narrowband representation at the long TIDMAD window
+
+_Written 11 September 2026, **before** any T22 code was written and before any
+T22 stretch was opened. Machine-readable companion:
+[`mlst_protocol_2026-09-11-t22-stage0.json`](mlst_protocol_2026-09-11-t22-stage0.json),
+which is the single configuration source the runner reads. Design of record:
+[`MLST_EXPERIMENT_PROGRAMME.md` §II.T22](MLST_EXPERIMENT_PROGRAMME.md). This
+document resolves audit items (a)–(g) of
+[the Part II phase report §9](../reviews/2026-09-11-experiment-phase-report.md)
+and items 1–7 of the remote upgrade prompt; it does not change any success
+criterion._
+
+## 0. Why this stage exists
+
+T10–T12 evaluated a rank-2 whole-window subspace on TIDMAD at `w = 65536` and
+found **no useful recovery**: the combined contrasts against both usefulness
+references included zero, and a no-denoising bin read beat EMPCA by
+−1.19e−02 [−1.31e−02, −1.08e−02]. The diagnosed mechanism was dimensional: at
+`w = 65536` the real-view dimension is `p = 65536` against `n = 350` fit
+windows, `p/n = 187`, and the Marchenko–Pastur top-eigenvalue inflation is
+≈ 216× the noise level while the injected tone's bin power is only 25× it.
+
+T22 removes exactly that one factor. The window length, endpoint, labels,
+calibration, rank, baselines, bootstrap and reporting are the T10–T12 ones; the
+only change is the space the rank-2 subspace is fitted in, which becomes the
+real and imaginary parts of the `B` unitary-DFT bins centred on the injection
+bin (`2B ≤ 34` coordinates against the same 350 fit windows).
+
+**What a positive result would and would not mean.** A positive T22 does not
+rescue whole-window recovery, and it is not independent-file replication: the
+hold-out is new *time* in files already examined in T10–T12. A negative or
+inconclusive T22 is a complete outcome and is reported as such.
+
+## 1. Two recorded freezes
+
+| freeze | when | what it fixes | file |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| stage 0 | before any code, before any stretch is opened | allocation, representation, estimators, selection rule, admissibility, eligibility branches, dependence policy, inference, multiplicity, budget, output schema | this document + the JSON |
+| selected band | after development, before any hold-out outcome is read | the band `B`, the two block lengths, the dependence verdict, the file roles, all input and code hashes, the fit count spent so far | `reviews/2026-09-11-PREDECLARED_T22.md` |
+
+"Before any file opens" is defined operationally as **before any hold-out
+outcome is read**. The characterisation stage reads only the 64
+transfer-calibration windows of each hold-out stretch and reports no method
+outcome, so running it before the band freeze does not expose an outcome.
+
+## 2. Allocation and splits
+
+`w = 65536`, rank 2, guard 16 384 samples.
+
+| block | windows | samples | offset in the stretch |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| transfer calibration | 64 | 4 194 304 | 0 |
+| guard | — | 16 384 | 4 194 304 |
+| fit | 350 | 22 937 600 | 4 210 688 |
+| guard | — | 16 384 | 27 148 288 |
+| evaluation | 300 | 19 660 800 | 27 164 672 |
+| **stretch** | | **46 825 472** (4.6825 s) | |
+
+The runner derives the two offsets and the stretch length from the window
+counts and asserts them against the declared numbers, so the JSON cannot drift
+from the code.
+
+## 3. Data roles — temporal hold-out, not file replication
+
+**Hold-out.** Files `0012`–`0019`, one stretch each starting at sample
+**37 027 840** = 36 995 072 (the T10 stretch end) + 2 × 16 384, ending at
+83 853 312. Every file is 2 000 000 000 samples, so the stretch is well inside
+each. T10–T12 read `[0, 36 995 072)` of these files; the T22 stretch begins
+32 768 samples later, so **there is no overlap**. All eight were
+eligible-coupled at `w = 65536` in the T10 characterisation. This is a temporal
+hold-out on files already examined; it is not independent-file replication and
+is never written as such.
+
+Validation = the first three hold-out files in index order whose T22
+characterisation is eligible-coupled. Final test = every hold-out file not in
+validation. The two sets are disjoint by construction and validation outcomes
+never enter final-test summaries.
+
+**Development (amendment A1).** At `w = 65536` only one of the three original
+development files was eligible-coupled in the T10 characterisation (`0010`;
+`0000` uncoupled, `0005` chirped), which would have left the band-selection rule
+with a single input. The development set is therefore six stretches, in this
+declared priority order:
+
+| order | file | start | T10 role |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `abra_validation_0010.h5` | 7 097 152 | development |
+| 2 | `abra_validation_0008.h5` | 0 | validation |
+| 3 | `abra_validation_0009.h5` | 0 | validation |
+| 4 | `abra_validation_0011.h5` | 0 | validation |
+| 5 | `abra_validation_0000.h5` | 7 097 152 | development |
+| 6 | `abra_validation_0005.h5` | 7 097 152 | development |
+
+The three added files were fully exposed in T10 and are **not** among the T22
+hold-out files, so adding them spends no hold-out. The full band grid runs on
+the first four stretches in this order whose T22 characterisation is
+eligible-coupled; all six carry the `B = 1` identity control.
+
+## 4. Representation and the identity control
+
+For a stretch with injection bin `k_inj`, the learned space is the isometric
+real view of the `B` unitary-rFFT bins centred on `k_inj` — `2B` real
+coordinates with the `√2` factor on interior bins, so that the diagonal weight
+`1/N_k` applied to both coordinates of a bin is exactly the noise-whitening
+metric. Every band bin must be interior: DC and Nyquist carry one real
+coordinate each and can never enter a band. Band-PCA and band-EMPCA receive
+**identical** bins, rank, fit windows and preprocessing, and differ only in the
+metric. Whitening uses the diagonal Fourier bin powers of 256 science-file noise
+windows.
+
+`B = 1` is the **single-bin identity control**: two real coordinates, so a
+rank-2 projector is the identity and band-PCA = band-EMPCA = bin read exactly.
+The runner asserts this to a relative `1e-12` on every development stretch and
+aborts the stage on failure. `B = 1` is excluded from selecting a learned
+representation.
+
+Estimators, unchanged from T10–T12: `zero`, `calibration-mean`, `raw-bin`
+(the bin read), `quadrature-OF`, band-`pca`, band-`empca`, `wiener`,
+`shrinkage-cal`. Only `pca` and `empca` see the band; the other six are exactly
+the T10–T12 ones, so the comparison isolates the representation.
+
+## 5. Band selection (development only) — audit item (c)
+
+Candidates `B ∈ {3, 5, 9, 17}`.
+
+**Statistic.** Per selection stretch `d`, `Δ_d(B)` is the observed mean paired
+squared-error contrast `mean_i [ e²_i(bin read) − e²_i(band-EMPCA) ]` over that
+stretch's 300 evaluation windows, in readout physical-amplitude units.
+`m(B)` is the **equal-stretch mean** of `Δ_d(B)` — the same equal-unit
+aggregation the primary estimand uses.
+
+**Resampling.** 2000 replicates, seed 20260911. One replicate draws, per
+selection stretch, one circular-block resample of its calibration windows and
+one of its evaluation windows, refits `ĝ` and every calibration-dependent
+estimator, and then recomputes `Δ_d(B)` for **every candidate from the same
+resampled indices**, so candidates are paired inside the replicate and their
+differences are not inflated by independent resampling noise. `sd(B)` is the
+bootstrap standard deviation of the replicate value of `m(B)`.
+
+**Rule.** Let `B*` maximise `m(B)` over the admissible candidates (ties → the
+smaller `B`) and let `s = sd(B*)`. The selected band is the **smallest**
+admissible candidate with `m(B) ≥ m(B*) − s`. The smallest-`B` search resolves
+ties by construction.
+
+**Admissibility**, required on *every* selection stretch:
+
+1. `B ≥ 3` (the identity control is not a learned band);
+2. every band bin is interior;
+3. no second characterised line inside the band — no band bin other than
+   `k_inj` carries an excess over its **predicted Dirichlet leakage** larger
+   than 0.1 of the line bin power. Comparing against the predicted skirt rather
+   than against the raw neighbour power is what keeps the main line's own
+   leakage from rejecting every wide band;
+4. `2B ≤ n_fit/10 = 35`.
+
+**Exceptions.** No admissible candidate → `blocked-no-admissible-band`; no
+eligible-coupled development stretch → `blocked-no-eligible-development-stretch`.
+In either case `selected_band = null`, validation and the final test do not run,
+and all three verdicts are reported as not evaluable. Both branches are in the
+code, are exercised by tests, and are not a licence to retune.
+
+All five candidates are scored on the full-grid stretches, so the report shows
+what the inadmissible ones would have given; only admissible ones enter the
+argmax.
+
+## 6. Calibration-only determination — audit item (d)
+
+`k_inj` is determined once per stretch, from the transfer-calibration windows of
+the **reference channel only**, by the frozen T10 characterisation function; it
+is never re-estimated per evaluation window and the evaluation block is never
+given to it. The declared thresholds are the T10 ones: prominence ≥ 1000,
+no second line within ±500 Hz at ≥ 10 % of the main line, drift ≤ 0.5 bins over
+the stretch, readout line SNR ≥ 1, reference line SNR ≥ 100 for the
+readout-unit target. Because the T22 stretch is 1.27× longer than T10's, the
+drift test is correspondingly stricter — that is intended and is not adjusted.
+
+Sub-bin offset `δ`, the Dirichlet attenuation `D(δ)`, the leakage-sensitivity of
+the off-line floor, the split-half gain agreement and the errors-in-variables
+note are all recorded per stretch. Transfer uncertainty enters the inference
+through the joint bootstrap, which refits `ĝ`, the calibration mean and the
+shrinkage weight inside every replicate.
+
+## 7. Dependence and precision — audit item (b)
+
+Evaluation block candidates `(1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32)` — amendment A2, made possible
+by the 300-window allocation, which leaves `⌊300/32⌋ = 9` complete blocks at the
+top of the grid. Calibration candidates `(1, 2, 4, 8)`. Minimum 5 blocks;
+stabilisation ratio 1.15; the T10 plateau rule, which never accepts the largest
+candidate as a plateau.
+
+Nine complete blocks is **the same limiting count as T10's 150/16**. The longer
+evaluation set widens the diagnosable range; it does not solve the dependence
+problem, and this protocol does not claim that it does.
+
+**Declared precision policy (amendment A3).** If the aggregate development
+verdict is `inconclusive`, **all three** benefit verdicts — limited recovery,
+denoising benefit and metric contribution — are withheld and reported as
+inconclusive. T10 withheld only the "useful" verdict; the audit required the
+condition to apply to every benefit claim, and it now does. A
+`stabilised-at-endpoint` verdict permits the verdicts but is flagged in every
+summary.
+
+## 8. Inference and the three claims — audit items (b), (f) and prompt items 5–6
+
+**Per file.** Joint circular-block bootstrap (calibration and evaluation
+windows resampled together, `ĝ` refitted per replicate), 2000 replicates, seed
+20260911, 95 % percentile interval, with the calibration-only component
+reported beside it.
+
+**Primary combined estimand.** The **equal-file mean** of the per-file
+contrasts over the eligible final-test files, with a **two-stage percentile
+bootstrap over files** (10 000 replicates, seed 20260911): each replicate
+resamples files with replacement and, within each drawn file, draws one value
+from that file's stored joint-bootstrap replicate array. This is how within-file
+calibration and block uncertainty enters the combined interval. The equal-file
+choice is the 11 September amendment, made because in T11/T12 file `0019`
+carried 98.65 % of the inverse-variance weight, so the weighted estimand was one
+file.
+
+**Secondary sensitivities**, always reported, never the headline:
+inverse-variance with Cochran's Q, I² and every file's weight share;
+DerSimonian–Laird random effects; the equal-file mean with a Student-t interval
+on the point estimates alone.
+
+**Small final-test count.** At most five files, possibly fewer. With fewer than
+four eligible files the combined interval is labelled **indicative only** and the
+per-file verdicts carry the conclusion. The number of files is stated beside
+every combined number.
+
+**Multiplicity.** The three claims form one declared family, controlled by
+**Holm–Bonferroni step-down at familywise level 0.05**. Two-sided bootstrap
+p-values come from the file-level bootstrap with the `(r+1)/(R+1)` continuity
+correction; the limited-recovery claim takes the larger of its two constituent
+p-values, because it requires both contrasts. A claim is declared only when
+its Holm-adjusted p < 0.05 **and** its 95 % interval excludes zero in EMPCA's
+favour **and** the dependence verdict is not inconclusive. Unadjusted intervals
+and raw p-values are reported beside the adjusted decisions. Per-file verdicts
+are descriptive and are not multiplicity-adjusted.
+
+**The three verdicts, reported separately; none implies another.**
+
+| verdict | contrast(s) |
+|---|---|
+| limited recovery | Δ(zero, band-EMPCA) **and** Δ(calibration-mean, band-EMPCA) |
+| denoising benefit | Δ(bin read, band-EMPCA) |
+| metric contribution | Δ(band-PCA, band-EMPCA) at the same selected `B` |
+
+Registered directions: bin read ≈ quadrature OF ≈ Wiener; band-EMPCA beats
+band-PCA. **No direction is registered for band-EMPCA versus the bin read** —
+that is the open question.
+
+## 9. Budget and fit accounting — prompt item 7
+
+A *fit* is one estimator instantiated on one (stretch, band) cell; the eight
+declared estimators are counted per cell, as in the T10–T12 accounting.
+
+| stage | cells | fits |
+|---|---|---|
+| characterisation (11 stretches) | — | 0 |
+| development, full band grid | 4 stretches × 5 bands | 160 |
+| development, identity control only | 2 stretches × 1 band | 16 |
+| validation | ≤ 3 files × 1 band | ≤ 24 |
+| final test | ≤ 5 files × 1 band | ≤ 40 |
+| **nominal total** | | **240** |
+| **hard cap** | | **250** |
+
+The nominal rises from the programme's 184 to 240 because of amendment A1; it
+stays inside the declared hard cap of 250, which is **not** raised. The runner
+enumerates a stage's fits before opening any data file and refuses to start if
+the running total would exceed the cap. Because the final test takes every
+hold-out file not assigned to validation, the hold-out total is 64 fits however
+the roles fall.
+
+Resampling is not fitting and never counts against the cap; it is reported in
+its own row: 2000 per-file joint replicates, 2000 band-selection paired
+replicates, 10 000 file-level replicates, 400 block-variance-curve replicates.
+Smoke runs use seed base 999 000 001, are marked non-scientific, and are logged
+in the exposure record with their own count.
+
+## 10. Reconciliation with the server checkout — audit item (g)
+
+The T10–T12 implementation on the execution host is
+`experiments/mlst2026/t10_tidmad_runner.py` with
+`experiments/mlst2026/tidmad_endpoint.py`, at EXP `a7125ea` on branch
+`mlst/exp-phase-20260910`, and its archive `results/mlst_2026-09-10/` verifies
+against its `RESULTS_SHA256` (all ten stage outputs). T22 imports that endpoint
+module unchanged and adds `experiments/mlst2026/tidmad_band.py`; the local
+`tidmad_window_sweep.py` is **not** used and is not equivalent. Raw-data root
+`/ceph/dwong/paper1_dataset/tidmad/raw`. Every instrument file read is hashed
+once in the characterisation stage and cited by digest thereafter.
+
+## 11. Amendments, all made before the affected outcomes
+
+| id | what | why |
+|---|---|---|
+| A1 | development set 3 → 6 stretches; full grid on the first four eligible in the declared order; nominal fits 184 → 240 (cap unchanged) | only one original development file is eligible-coupled at `w = 65536`, so the selection rule would have had a single input; the added files are already exposed and are not hold-out |
+| A2 | evaluation block grid gains `32` | the 300-window allocation exists precisely so that `b = 32` leaves nine complete blocks |
+| A3 | the dependence withholding rule applies to all three benefit verdicts; the primary combined interval becomes a two-stage bootstrap | audit item (b) and prompt item 5 |
+
+None of these changes the hold-out set, the offsets, the estimators, the
+endpoint, the selection rule or any success criterion.
+
+## 12. Outputs
+
+`results/t22_2026-09-11/T22_<stage>_v1/` containing `t22_<stage>.json`,
+`t22_<stage>_draws.npz` (the per-file joint-bootstrap replicate arrays, so every
+interval and p-value can be recomputed without the instrument data) and
+`RESULTS_SHA256`. The freeze output embeds the whole stage-0 protocol, so the
+archive is self-describing.
