+| development fits spent | 176 of the 250 hard cap |
+| planned hold-out fits | 24 (validation) + 40 (final test) = 64; total 240 |
+
+### How B = 9 was selected
+
+The declared rule is "the smallest admissible candidate whose equal-stretch mean
+Δ(bin read, band-EMPCA) is within one paired-bootstrap standard deviation of the
+best candidate".  On the four eligible-coupled development stretches:
+
+| B | admissible | equal-stretch mean | paired-bootstrap sd | bootstrap 95 % CI |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 3 | yes | +0.004326 | 0.000575 | [0.003238, 0.005495] |
+| 5 | yes | +0.005387 | 0.000659 | [0.004088, 0.006656] |
+| 9 | yes | +0.005636 | 0.000710 | [0.004217, 0.007012] |
+| 17 | yes | **+0.006109** (best) | 0.000677 | [0.004772, 0.007387] |
+
+Best candidate B = 17; threshold = 0.006109 − 0.000677 = **0.005432**; the
+smallest admissible candidate at or above it is **B = 9** (B = 5 falls short at
+0.005387).  B = 1 is the identity control and is excluded from selection by the
+protocol.
+
+### The B = 1 identity control
+
+Asserted on **all six** development stretches at a relative tolerance of
+10⁻¹²: band-PCA = band-EMPCA = bin read.  The measured Δ(bin read, band-EMPCA)
+at B = 1 was between −1.2 × 10⁻¹⁸ and +2.9 × 10⁻¹⁷ on the six stretches, i.e.
+numerically zero; the runner aborts the stage on failure.
+
+### The dependence verdict, and what it does
+
+The aggregate evaluation variance curve over the development stretches is
+**still rising at the largest usable block**: adjacent ratios
+[2.089, 2.072, 1.731, 2.128, 1.745] over b = [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32], with
+V(32)/V(16) = 1.745, so the declared plateau rule returns **inconclusive**.
+Per-curve the picture is mixed (112 stabilised, 107 inconclusive, 1 at the
+endpoint); the declared decision is taken on the aggregated (maximum-normalised)
+curve, which is conservative by construction.  The calibration curve is
+inconclusive as well (b = 8).
+
+**By amendment A3, declared before development, an inconclusive dependence
+verdict withholds all three benefit verdicts** — limited recovery, denoising
+benefit and metric contribution — not only the limited-recovery one.  The
+hold-out stages still run once each and the estimates, intervals, p-values and
+per-file rows are all archived and reported; what is withheld is the positive
+verdict.  This is the outcome the audit anticipated: 300 evaluation windows at
+block 32 leave nine complete blocks, the same limiting count as T10's 150/16, so
+the longer evaluation set widened the diagnosable range without resolving the
+dependence problem.
+
