+## 6. What each verdict will say
+
+| verdict | contrast(s) | declared decision rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| limited recovery | Δ(zero, band-EMPCA) **and** Δ(cal-mean, band-EMPCA) | both point estimates favour EMPCA, both 95 % equal-file intervals exclude zero, Holm-adjusted p < 0.05, dependence not inconclusive |
+| denoising benefit | Δ(bin read, band-EMPCA) | as above for the single contrast |
+| metric contribution | Δ(band-PCA, band-EMPCA) at B = 9 | as above |
+
+Because the frozen dependence verdict **is** inconclusive, every one of the
+three will be reported as `inconclusive` whatever the estimates show.  That is
+the declared rule applying as written, decided before the hold-out was opened,
+and it is not revisited after the fact.  Registered directions: bin read ≈
+quadrature OF ≈ Wiener; band-EMPCA better than band-PCA; **no direction is
+registered for band-EMPCA against the bin read** — that remains the open
+question.
+
+## 7. What a failed validation does not permit
+
+A failed validation does not permit retuning the band, the block lengths, the
+estimators or the criterion on those outcomes.  Crashes and retries are logged
+separately from statistical evaluations; the final test is executed once.
